on-arrival: {!
Q.formation_tusk_suit_done = 1;
Q.ko_relation += 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 6;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline = "Tusk enters government with PSL's help and a harder tone";
!}

= The suit of office

Once the arithmetic is clear, Tusk stops sounding like a man who only wants to
win an election. He begins to speak like a prime minister who knows the cabinet
must be carried by a coalition that is less a partner than a reluctant
concession. KO still claims the premiership, but the government is already
wearing the smell of PSL's bargaining power and the Palace's patience.

- @formation_hundred_days: Continue

@formation_hundred_days
# prose-audit: Grade B — Correctly shows the hundred days being rationed by the coalition contract before the clock starts, in one well-judged paragraph. Also a read-and-continue with no choice of its own.
title: The hundred-days programme is rationed before it begins
new-page: true
view-if: formation_tusk_suit_done = 1 and formation_hundred_days_done = 0 and president_name = "Andrzej Duda" and democratic_candidate = "Donald Tusk" and candidate_psl_votes > 0 and democratic_votes < 276
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
on-arrival: {!
Q.formation_hundred_days_done = 1;
Q.ko_poll_momentum -= 0.2;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 4;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.news_headline = "The hundred-days programme is narrowed by coalition strain";
!}

= Before the clock starts

The cabinet has not governed for three months yet, but the coalition contract
already shows which hundred-days promises cannot survive intact. Every reform
is measured against PSL's price, the Palace's timetable and the number of
partners willing to own it. The campaign of clean deadlines enters office as a
programme of negotiated sequencing.

- @government_entry_gate: Continue

