@budget_vote_continue
view-if: left_in_government = 1
go-to: budget_passed if annual_budget_passed = 1; budget_crisis if annual_budget_passed = 0

@budget_passed
title: A budget and an ultimatum
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: government_delivery += 5; public_trust += 3; budget_cycle_year = 2026; next_budget_label = "December 2025"; ending_score += 18; coalition_break_threat = 1; date_label = "January 2025"; year = 2025; month = 1; month_name = "January"

= The vote does not end the year

PSL ministers approve the budget, then their parliamentary club demands a new
coalition annex on agriculture, religious schooling and conscience votes.
They threaten to leave if the annex is not signed. That rhythm—vote, threaten,
renegotiate—is not irrational. It is how a smaller, right-leaning partner
prevents **[+ ko_seats +]-seat KO** from treating it as an appendage.

- @coalition_break: Answer the PSL ultimatum

@budget_crisis
title: A defeated budget is not yet a fallen cabinet
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: government_delivery -= 8; public_trust -= 6; fiscal_stress += 12; coalition_break_threat = 1; psl_coalition_dissent += 8; ending_score -= 10

= The constitutional and political clocks diverge

The Sejm has rejected the bill. The cabinet may negotiate another text; the
President's power to shorten the term concerns failure to receive a budget
within the constitutional timetable, not this single defeat. Politically,
however, PSL calls the vote proof that the coalition agreement is exhausted.

- @budget_rescue
- @article160_open
- @constructive_motion

@budget_rescue
title: Reopen the budget and pay for a coalition rescue
subtitle: Spend 2 governing capacity. The revised bill still needs more yes than no.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Requires two remaining governing-capacity points.
on-arrival: {!
const sejmTotal = Math.max(1, Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460);
Q.budget -= 2;
Q.annual_budget_yes = Math.min(
    sejmTotal,
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.coalition_democratic_seats) || 0)
);
const fallbackRightNo =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.korona_seats) || 0) +
    (String(Q.social_patriot_list_committee || "") == "pis"
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.social_patriot_seats) || 0)
        : 0);
const rightNo = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.coalition_right_seats))
    ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.coalition_right_seats))
    : fallbackRightNo;
Q.annual_budget_no = Math.min(
    sejmTotal - Q.annual_budget_yes,
    rightNo
);
Q.annual_budget_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    sejmTotal - Q.annual_budget_yes - Q.annual_budget_no
);
Q.annual_budget_present =
    Q.annual_budget_yes + Q.annual_budget_no + Q.annual_budget_abstain;
Q.annual_budget_threshold = Q.annual_budget_no + 1;
Q.annual_budget_passed =
    Q.annual_budget_present >= Q.sejm_quorum_floor &&
    Q.annual_budget_yes > Q.annual_budget_no ? 1 : 0;
Q.government_delivery += Q.annual_budget_passed ? 2 : -2;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 5;
Q.coalition_break_threat = 1;
Q.news_headline = Q.annual_budget_passed
    ? "A revised budget survives inside the constitutional window"
    : "The revised budget still cannot command a simple majority";
!}
go-to: coalition_break

@coalition_break
title: PSL keeps a hand on the door
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1

= Coalition rupture as bargaining technology

The **[+ psl_seats +]-seat PSL club** votes on whether its ministers should resign. Its core
wants delivery, regional brokers want proof of autonomy and two conservatives
would prefer a right-wing partnership. Poland 2050 warns that a PSL rupture
could also rupture Third Way.

The cabinet has four lawful choices. It can concede, continue as a minority,
ask the Sejm for confidence under Article 160, or let opponents try the much
harder constructive vote under Article 158.

- @coalition_repair
- @coalition_minority
- @article160_open
- @constructive_motion

@coalition_repair
title: Sign the annex and keep PSL in cabinet
subtitle: Spend 2 governing capacity. Stability now, a larger conservative veto later.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Requires two remaining governing-capacity points.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; coalition_break_threat = 0; coalition_broken = 0; ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1; psl_coalition_dissent -= 15; psl_relation += 8; progressive_credibility -= 5; feminist_trust -= 5; razem_dissent += 7; coalition_status = "Four-party coalition with PSL annex"; ending_name = "The coalition survives its first budget"; ending_score += 15; news_headline = "PSL stays after winning a new coalition annex"
go-to: campaign_return if formation_continuous = 1; assessment if formation_continuous = 0

@coalition_minority
title: Accept PSL's resignation and continue as a minority
subtitle: A legal minority cabinet; every bill now needs abstentions or issue partners.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.coalition_broken = 1;
Q.coalition_break_threat = 0;
Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent = 100;
Q.coalition_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0);
Q.government_support_seats = Q.coalition_seats;
Q.coalition_status = "KO · Poland 2050 · Left minority cabinet";
const resignedPSLPortfolios = {
    economy: ["KO", "Borys Budka"],
    agriculture: ["KO", "Dorota Niedziela"],
    defence: ["KO", "Tomasz Siemoniak"]
};
for (const portfolio of Object.keys(resignedPSLPortfolios)) {
    if (Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] == "PSL") {
        Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] =
            resignedPSLPortfolios[portfolio][0];
        Q[portfolio + "_minister"] =
            resignedPSLPortfolios[portfolio][1];
    }
}
Q.psl_relation -= 18;
Q.government_delivery -= 5;
Q.ending_name = "A parliamentary minority";
Q.ending_score += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "PSL leaves and the cabinet continues without manufacturing a confidence vote";
!}
go-to: campaign_return if formation_continuous = 1; assessment if formation_continuous = 0

@article160_open
title: The prime minister asks for confidence
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1

= Article 160 — confidence by simple majority

The prime minister can request a confidence vote. More yes than no is enough
with quorum, so the cabinet can survive if PSL abstains while the right votes
against. If PSL joins the no lobby, the arithmetic can reverse.

- @confidence_rural_deal
- @confidence_minority_discipline
- @confidence_left_redline

@confidence_rural_deal
